        <body>
            <div xml:id="d999">

                <pb facs="0760" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 703.4112/7.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 1, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: With reference to my
                    letter of yesterday on the subject of the chargéship of United States interests
                    in Mexico, I beg to inform you that I have this morning heard from Sir L. Garden
                    that my telegram of the 23rd of April only reached him on the 29th and that he
                    at once notified to the Minister of Foreign Affairs the appointment of the
                    Brazilian Minister, and handed over American interests to the latter.</p>
                <p>Sir L. Garden adds that it will always be a great pleasure to him to lend to the
                    Brazilian Minister any assistance in his power.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil Spring Rice</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
